# Known-benign findings, pinned by exact fingerprint (commit:file:rule:line).
#
# gitleaks scans git *history*, while scripts/verify_local.sh greps the working tree. That gap
# is why commit 90795cf ("let the local gate's secret scan pass on this repository") made the
# local scan pass while the launch gate's gitleaks step still blocked on every run: it renamed
# the fixtures in the working tree to the FAKE convention, but the older commits still contain
# the strings they were renamed from.
#
# Every entry below was checked against the historical blob before being listed. They are
# synthetic test doubles that never authenticated anything:
#
#   tvly-CRASHTESTKEY0000000000      crash-injection provider fixture
#   sk-CRASHTESTKEY000000000         crash-injection provider fixture
#   tvly-A-CLIENTS-OWN-KEY-00000     asserts a caller-supplied key is refused
#   tvly-SOMEONE-ELSES-KEY-000000    asserts a foreign key is refused
#   Zx91ppQvNn02bLkeRt77 and friends  the redaction corpus in test_secrets.py, which must look
#                                     like credentials because proving they get redacted is the
#                                     entire point of that test
#
# Pinned by fingerprint rather than allowlisted by path or rule, deliberately: a path allowlist
# for tests/ would silently accept a real key pasted into a test tomorrow, whereas these
# entries stop matching the moment the content, file or line changes.
